  there's a subscription table at all, what the UI has to expose, and — most importantly — whether the default is
  silence or noise.

  - [1mExplicit watch[0m — a follow button per task. Precise, easy to reason about, no surprise notifications. Costs: an empty
    state problem. Nobody watches anything on day one, so the feature looks broken until people opt in. Changing this
    later is cheap.
  - [1mImplicit by involvement[0m — you're subscribed to tasks you created, were assigned, or commented on. Feels right
    immediately with zero user effort, and it's what most tools do. Costs: "why am I getting this?" moments, and you
    need an unsubscribe escape hatch anyway. Requires the task model to track creator/assignee from stage one — that
    part is [3mnot[0m cheap to retrofit.
  - [1mEverything in the workspace[0m — notify on all changes, let people filter. Trivially simple to build. Costs: unusable
    past a handful of people. This is the one that gets ripped out.
  - [1mImplicit + explicit override[0m — involvement subscribes you, and you can mute a task or watch one you're not involved
    in. Best behavior, most surface area.

  [1mMy recommendation: implicit by involvement, with an explicit mute/watch override — but build the implicit half first.[0m
  For a present, collaborating team, involvement is a genuinely good predictor, and it solves the empty-state problem
  that kills explicit-only. The override half is additive and can land in a second pass. The one thing I'd lock in now
  regardless: the task model carries [38;5;153mcreator[39m and [38;5;153massignee[39m from the start, because inferring involvement retroactively is
  the expensive mistake.
[38;5;246m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Subscription [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mHow does a user come to "care about" a task?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mImplicit, override later (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mCreator/assignee/commenter are subscribed automatically. Mute and manual-watch land in a second pass. Solves the [39m
     [38;5;246mempty-state problem with no user effort.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Implicit + override together
     [38;5;246mInvolvement subscribes you, plus mute/watch buttons in the same build. Best end state, more surface area in v1.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Explicit watch only
     [38;5;246mA follow button per task, nothing automatic. Precise and predictable, but nobody is subscribed to anything on day [39m
     [38;5;246mone.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Everything, filter later
     [38;5;246mNotify on all workspace changes. Simplest to build, degrades badly past a few users.[39m
  [38;5;246m5. Type something.[39m
